-- title:
--   Diamonds commute with the degeneracy map q ↦ qᵖ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup. Write $E =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of the rational function field `xHFunctionField M H` under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, and likewise $E' =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` at level $M/p$, where `infSubgroup` is the image of $H$ under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Let $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, let $x \in E$ and $u \in E'$, and assume that the Laurent series underlying $x$ is the image of that underlying $u$ under `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) p`, the ring homomorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ obtained by multiplying all exponents by $p$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$. Then the Laurent series underlying `diamondAutHBar M H d x` is the image under the same substitution of the Laurent series underlying `diamondAutHBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` $\bar d$ $u$, where $\bar d$ is the reduction of $d$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Here `diamondAutHBar M H d` denotes a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $E$ satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d`, chosen if one exists and the identity otherwise; that predicate requires that for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g$ having nonzero associated series, and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose upper-left entry reduces to $d$ modulo $M$, the value of $\sigma$ on (the image of) $f/g$ is the image of an element $y$ of `xHFunctionField M H` with $y \cdot (g \mid_k \gamma) = f \mid_k \gamma$ as $q$-expansions over $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the diamond operators with the degeneracy map $\tau \mapsto p\tau$, i.e. $q \mapsto q^p$, from level $M/p$ to level $M$, expressed on the geometric function fields inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$; classically it rests on the fact that conjugation by $\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$ carries $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ to an element of $\Gamma_0(M/p)$ with the same diagonal reduction. It is used, together with the generation of the level-$M$ field by the level-$M/p$ field and its $q \mapsto q^p$ image, in the commutation and square laws relating diamond operators to the Atkin–Lehner type automorphisms.
